-- title:
--   Vanishing in negative weight for mod-p modular functions
-- statement:
--   Let $p\ge 5$ be a prime, let $N\ge 1$ be an integer with $p\nmid N$, and let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$. Inside the field of formal Laurent series over $K$ consider the intermediate field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ K\ N$, the $K$-subfield generated by the two series `jqModC K` and `jqNModC K N` (the reductions of $j(q)$ and of $j(q^N)$). Let $m$ be a negative integer and let $G$ be an element of that field. Places are the objects of [`AlgebraicCurve.Place`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L22): valuation subrings of the field which contain the image of $K$, are proper, and are principal ideal rings; for such an $x$ and an element $f$, $x.\mathrm{ord}\, f$ is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation of $f$, and $x.\mathrm{evalAt}\, f$ is the residue of $f$ pulled back to $K$ when $f$ lies in the valuation subring, and $0$ otherwise. Write $w(x)=\mathrm{jWidth}(x.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\ K\ N))$, equal to $3$ if that residue is $0$, to $2$ if it is $1728$, and to $1$ otherwise, and let $\mathrm{placeWidth}\ N\ x$ be the natural-number quotient of $w(x)$ by the ramification invariant $\mathrm{placeRamificationJ}\ N\ x$ of $x$ over $j$. Assume: (i) for every place $x$ at which both $\mathrm{jGeomGen}\ K\ N$ and $\mathrm{jNGeomGen}\ K\ N$ lie in the valuation subring (the affine places), one has $0\le \mathrm{placeWidth}\ N\ x\cdot x.\mathrm{ord}\,G + m\,(w(x)-1)$; (ii) for every place $x$ with $x.\mathrm{ord}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\ K\ N)<0$, one has $m\cdot(-x.\mathrm{ord}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\ K\ N))\le x.\mathrm{ord}\,G$. Then $G=0$.
--
--   This is the vanishing statement for modular functions of negative weight in characteristic $p$: a function whose divisor is bounded below by the stack-theoretic weight-$m$ condition at the affine places and by the cusp bound must vanish, since for $m<0$ the forced zeros outweigh the allowed poles. It is used in the study of mod-$p$ modular forms of level $N$, where it is cited by [`ModPForms.mem_modPMod_sub_of_qP_mul_mem`](thm.html#ModPForms.mem_modPMod_sub_of_qP_mul_mem).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_eq_zero_of_forall_stackOrd_nonneg_of_forall_le_ord_of_neg.lean

